This product is a Cangjie (仓颉) / HarmonyOS port of the EU Digital Identity
Wallet ISO/IEC 18013-5 §9 security library for Swift:

    eudi-lib-ios-iso18013-security
    Copyright (c) European Commission
    Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0
    https://github.com/eu-digital-identity-wallet/eudi-lib-ios-iso18013-security

The security layer (session encryption / ECDH+HKDF+AES-GCM, device & reader
authentication, MSO validation, SecureArea implementations) is reimplemented
in Cangjie with the original Swift sources used as the reference implementation.
The x509certificates portion of the Swift library was migrated into a separate
module (eudi_lib_x509) and is consumed from there, not re-implemented here.

This product depends on and/or bundles the following third-party software:

  - eudi_lib_mdoc_data_model (Apache-2.0; pinned third_party clone) — COSE /
    CoseKey / MobileSecurityObject / SecureArea protocol / data types.
  - eudi_lib_core_crypto (pinned third_party clone) — ECDH P-256 (HUKS),
    AES-GCM, HKDF, digest, ECDSA primitives.
  - eudi_lib_x509 (Apache-2.0; pinned third_party clone) — certificate chain
    validation.
  - eudi_lib_cbor (Apache-2.0; pinned third_party clone) — CBOR encoding.
  - cangjie-stdx 1.1.3.1 (Apache-2.0) — bundled under entry/libs/stdx/.
  - OpenSSL runtime libraries and libsecurec.so, bundled under
    entry/libs/arm64-v8a/ for on-device stdx.crypto / HUKS execution.

